ack  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibrofatty breast tissue  with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast final shaved deep margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm portion of tan yellow fibrofatty tissue  with a black stitch along one aspect  The stitched aspect is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal gray hemorrhagic tan yellow adipose tissue  with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast final shaved inferior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm portion of gray white to tan red fibrofatty tissue  with a black stitch along one aspect  The stitched aspect is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal focally dense gray white fibrous tissue  with no discrete lesion or other gross abnormality  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1 AND  1A   LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE   NO EVIDENCE OF LOBULAR CARCINOMA  AWAIT PERMANENTS  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained 